# Maintainer-local notes and tooling state. Never committed.
# Both paths are ignored so that a tool which auto-creates either one
# cannot accidentally publish its contents. Maintainer tooling config is
# excluded per-clone via .git/info/exclude rather than named here.
.claude/
private/

# Stray scratch files
CLAUDE.md.tmp
*.tmp
pytest-cache-files-*

# Operator-local bootloader launcher scratch copies (with hardcoded
# agent tokens / pubkeys / state-dir overrides). The shipped reference
# is at examples/run_bootloader_example.py — env-var-only, never holds
# a secret. Operators commonly cp that to the repo root and edit in
# real values for fast iteration; gitignore guards against accidental
# commit of the operator-local copy.
/run_bootloader.py
/run_bootloader_*.py

# v0.4 phone app (MAUI Blazor) — source tracked under /phone/, build
# artifacts (bin/, obj/, .vs/, NuGet packages, Android APK staging,
# iOS DerivedData) are not. The /phone/ folder itself stays in the
# repo so contributors can build the app; only its compile outputs
# are ignored.
/phone/**/bin/
/phone/**/obj/
/phone/**/.vs/
/phone/**/packages/
/phone/**/Properties/launchSettings.json
/phone/**/AppPackages/
/phone/**/Resources/Raw/.gitkeep
/phone/**/*.user
/phone/**/*.suo

# Phone-app credential ceremony artifacts. Each operator deploying
# Recto runs their own Apple Developer Program + Firebase Console
# ceremony per dev-tools/README.md; the resulting credential files are
# operator-specific and never get checked in. Forkers regenerate them
# for their own bundle ID + Firebase project. Public Recto repo carries
# only the wire-up that READS these files; the values stay on the
# operator's machine.
/phone/**/dev-tools/.fcm-service-account.json
/phone/**/dev-tools/.apns-auth-key.p8
/phone/**/dev-tools/.credentials.md
/phone/**/google-services.json
# Catch-alls so future credential files of these shapes are protected
# even if the directory layout changes:
/phone/**/*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
/phone/**/*.p8
/phone/**/AuthKey_*.p8
/phone/**/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Operator-specific launchers. Kept as a PATTERN with the shipped examples
# allowlisted back in, rather than one line per private launcher: an ignore
# rule naming a file that is not in the tree publishes that file's name, and
# the name is the whole disclosure. Same shape as the docs/_config.yml
# allowlist -- fail-closed by default, and adding a private launcher needs no
# edit here at all.
examples/run_bootloader_*.py
!examples/run_bootloader_consumer.py
!examples/run_bootloader_example.py

# Code-signing artifacts (operator-local, never commit)
*.certSigningRequest
*.cer
*.mobileprovision

# Android signing artifacts (banked 2026-05-21 alongside the Android
# signing PropertyGroup in Recto.csproj). The upload keystore is
# operator-local at ~/keystores/recto-upload.keystore on MAC and
# MUST NEVER enter any repo. AABs are build artifacts (the signed
# upload artifact for Play Console); they're large + per-build and
# don't belong in the tree either. PKCS12 .p12 files are the canonical
# Android keystore extension on modern toolchains; legacy .jks (Java
# KeyStore) likewise. Defense-in-depth: catch any of these shapes
# anywhere in the tree, not just the keystore directory.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
**/keystores/**
*.aab

# Signed binaries: 218 MB across 5 AAB/APK. Too large for git, and recoverable
# (Play retains uploaded bundles; they rebuild from source). NEEDS AN OFF-MACHINE
# BACKUP, not a commit.
/build-outputs

# MUST NEVER BE PUBLISHED. These were tracked for 26 minutes on 2026-08-17
# (cabbdf8) and the commit was scrubbed from history the same day. Operator
# ruling: store art does not ship in a public tree.
#
#   - It hands a cloner PIXEL-PERFECT COUNTERFEIT MATERIAL -- icon, feature
#     graphic, and real UI shots -- which is precisely how a fake listing is
#     made convincing.
#   - It publishes a DEVELOPMENT TIMELINE the stores never show: V2 -> V3,
#     Android and iPhone, dated by commit. A trail of crumbs.
#   - Git serves ORIGINALS, in bulk, by API, forever. A store listing serves
#     resized images behind a UI. Those are not the same exposure.
#
# THE ARGUMENT THAT WAS WRONG, kept because it is subtle: "already public on
# the store listings, so tracking them discloses nothing." A listing serves ONE
# Store-submission images and icons are maintainer artifacts, not source.
# They are backed up outside this repository; a public tree is a
# publication channel, not a backup.
/app-store-screenshots
/icons

# Operator-config + runtime state that must NEVER land in the public tree.
# Consumer-identifying values live operator-side only; this tree must read
# like a generic project a stranger could fork and run.
# agents.json / devices-pair-consumers.json are per-deployment registries
# (canonical copies live in the operator's installed-state dir, not the
# repo clone); events/ is the folder-drop event-bus output. Repo-root
# copies exist on some hosts as legacy bind-mount sources — gitignored
# so they are structurally uncommittable.
# GLOB, not exact path (2026-08-16). `/agents.json` matched the live file and
# NOTHING ELSE: an `agents.json.bak-20260815043413` sat UNTRACKED and UNIGNORED
# in a public tree for a day, one `git add -A` away from publishing the
# per-deployment agent tokens. The comment above claimed "structurally
# uncommittable" — a claim the pattern did not deliver, and the file that
# disproved it was created by a rotation ceremony that made its own backup.
# A rule that names one filename does not cover the files a tool derives FROM
# that filename. The trailing * is the whole fix. `examples/agents.json.example`
# is unaffected: these patterns are root-anchored (verified, not assumed).
/agents.json*
/devices-pair-consumers.json*
/events/
